        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scientists studied 105 students between the ages of eight and nine. Twenty-three trained dogs and their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "trainers",
            "ref": "v-trainer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " also took part in the experiment. The children "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "were divided into",
            "ref": "v-be-divided-into"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " three groups. The students in the first group spent 20 minutes with a dog and its trainer. They did this twice a week for four weeks. The second group spent the same amount of time doing "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "relaxation",
            "ref": "v-relaxation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " exercises. The last group did neither of these things."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During this time, the scientists recorded the students’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "cortisol levels",
            "zh": "皮质醇水平"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Cortisol is a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "stress hormone",
            "zh": "激素"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The more stressed you feel, the more cortisol you will have in your body. What did the scientists find? Both the second and third groups showed rises in cortisol levels. The first group, however, showed no big "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "increase",
            "ref": "v-increase"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". And the children had the lowest cortisol levels right after playing with the dogs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But here comes the next question: Is 20 minutes of playtime with a dog the best amount of time? Scientists are going to keep working to find out the answer."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
